# Hawaii 2026 Unified Project Standards

## Project Overview
- This is an Eleventy static site: source in `hawaii-2026/src/`, generated output in `hawaii-2026/_site/`.
- Primary pages are home (`index.njk`), about (`about.njk`), and story (`story/index.njk`).
- Reusable UI lives in `src/_includes/partials/`; base shell in `src/_includes/layouts/base.njk`.
- Deployment/docs are in `openshift/` and `docs/`; do not mix app code into those folders.

## File Ownership and Structure
- Treat `src/` as source of truth; treat `_site/` as build output.
- Do not implement long-term fixes directly in `_site/` unless explicitly requested.
- Keep assets organized by type in `src/assets/images/{logos,layouts,profile,landscape}`.
- Keep page scripts in `src/js/` and styles in `src/css/` (shared in `components.css`, page-specific in `home.css`, `about.css`, `story.css`).

## Styling Consistency (All Assets and Pages)
- Reuse existing color/font/spacing patterns and CSS variables before introducing new values.
- Prefer shared component classes and patterns from `src/css/components.css`.
- Scope page overrides with page classes (e.g., `.page-about ...`) to avoid cross-page regressions.
- Keep image behavior consistent: explicit `width`/`height` in markup when known, sensible `object-fit`/`object-position`.
- Preserve visual consistency for buttons, cards, hero blocks, dividers, and footer/nav treatments.

## Naming Conventions
- Use kebab-case for file names and CSS classes (`hero__media`, `profile-card__avatar`).
- Keep BEM-like class naming already used in this project (`block__element`, `block--modifier`).
- Use clear, semantic identifiers for JS hooks (`data-*` attributes) and avoid ambiguous names.

## Navigation Standards
- Keep primary nav structure/labels/ordering consistent across pages.
- Reuse `home-nav.njk` and existing nav JS behavior rather than duplicating nav markup.
- Preserve route style consistency (existing root-relative links and trailing-slash behavior already in repo).

## Accessibility Standards
- Use semantic headings in order (`h1` -> `h2` -> `h3`) without skipping levels.
- Provide meaningful `alt` text for content images; empty `alt` for decorative images only.
- Ensure interactive controls are keyboard accessible and have clear labels.
- Keep ARIA minimal and correct; prefer native HTML semantics first.
- Preserve color contrast and readable text sizes across breakpoints.

## Git Collaboration Standards
- Make small, focused changes tied to a single intent.
- Do not rewrite or revert unrelated user changes.
- Keep commit messages concise and purpose-first when committing.
- Call out assumptions, risks, and follow-up tasks in PR summaries.
- Never commit secrets, generated junk, or environment files.

## Agent Working Rules
- Before editing, check for an existing partial/style/script pattern to extend.
- Prefer minimal diffs over broad refactors unless explicitly requested.
- After substantive changes, verify impacted pages and responsive behavior.
- When a quick patch is applied in `_site/`, mirror the durable fix in `src/`.
